From e5ddf937f7561f55867b4ca32dfc5061749b4adf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:31:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Batch: stationary non linear heat transfer by kernels

The kernels computing the gradients, the inner forces and the tangent
operator (assembled, diagonal, action without assembly) support the
stationary non linear heat transfer behaviours (temperature gradient,
heat flux), in 3D, plane strain and plane stress:

- GradientsKind: TEMPERATURE_GRADIENT_3D and TEMPERATURE_GRADIENT_2D,
  detected from the gradients, the thermodynamic forces and the tangent
  operator blocks of the behaviour; getUnknownsSize (one for the
  temperature) is separated from getSpaceDimension in the kernels and their
  host parts; getTangentOperatorBlocksSize includes the derivative of the
  heat flux with respect to the temperature;
- the derivatives of the heat flux with respect to the temperature,
  multiplied by the values of the shape functions, are added to the
  stiffness matrices, to their diagonals and to the action of the tangent
  operator;
- the values of the unknowns at the integration points are computed with
  their derivatives when a behaviour integrator requires them
  (requiresUnknownsValuesForKernels), gathered for each material
  (getUnknownsValues) and copied in the temperature, external state
  variable of the behaviour, by the new method
  setExternalStateVariablesFromUnknownsValues of the generated heat
  transfer behaviour integrators (and of the code generator).

The tangent operator of the heat transfer behaviours is negative definite
(j = -k grad(T)): with the diagonal of the essential degrees of freedom
set to one, the conjugate gradient does not apply; the test uses GMRES.

Tests: HeatTransferKernelsTest (batches and kernels, assembled and without
assembly, with and without prediction, 3D and plane strain, behaviours of
the generic and generic-parallel interfaces, sequential, two processes,
debug device and GPU, compared to the integration point by point to 1e-10;
mutations of the external state variable and of the temperature blocks
detected). With the kernels forced, the heat transfer tests now pass (the
micromorphic behaviours remain refused).
